        "shortCode": "Dd3_LR_T4Oz",
        "caption": "@adamgrant and I loved talking with @angelalduckworth about her new book, “Situated.”\n\nBig takeaway:\n\n“To stay motivated through the countless hours of practice that separate amateurs from experts, grit is necessary but not sufficient. The situation also matters—and to an astonishing degree:\n\nCulture matters.\nMentors matter.\nTeammates matter.\nEven the objects in your personal space matter.\n\nHow you think about your goals and what you’re willing to do to achieve them depends on both you and your situation.”\n\nI also loved our conversation about billboards - those signs we post around our spaces as reminders of what’s important. It reminds of why I like to write in a room where my children’s art is hanging. The kids’ art is my favorite art and it’s imperfect and honest. Grit is great, but I also need the environment to say, “Have fun. Just start.”\n\nTo watch or listen to the episode, head to YouTube or wherever you listen to podcasts.",
