        "shortCode": "Dc1w8rHzGlS",
        "caption": "Grateful for a mother who warned her daughters about the price she paid for trying to conform to nice girl culture in the 1950’s. We didn’t know all of the details of her wounds, but we fully understood the depth of her pain. \n\nWhen she died she had framed pictures of Gloria Steinem and Angela Davis over her desk.\n \nQuote: Gloria Steinem’s remarks at the National Organization for Women’s March for the Equal Rights Amendment, Washington, D.C., July 9, 1978, as reported in James Lardner and Neil Henry, “Over 40,000 ERA Backers March,” Washington Post, July 10, 1978\n\n📸 Warren K. Leffler",
